---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Spoiler } from "astro-ink";
---
<Base title="Spoiler">
  <div class="docs-page">
    <h1>Spoiler</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">
      Long text, clamped to a few lines, with an honest way out. No fade
      tricks hiding the rest.
    </p>

    <h2>Example</h2>
    <div class="docs-example" style="display: grid;">
      <span class="docs-example-label" aria-hidden="true">Example</span>
      <Spoiler lines={3}>
        <p>Plot twist the first: the butler refactored the codebase at midnight, and every test passed on the first run. Plot twist the second: the code review found nothing to complain about. Plot twist the third: it shipped on a Friday and the weekend stayed quiet.</p>
      </Spoiler>
    </div>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;Spoiler lines=&#123;3&#125;&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Plot twist the first...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/Spoiler&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>Props</h2>
    <table class="docs-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>lines</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>3</code></td><td>Visible lines when closed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>showLabel / hideLabel</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>Show more / Show less</code></td><td>Toggle text.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <ul class="docs-list">
      <li>Toggle is a button with <code>aria-expanded</code>.</li>
      <li>Full text stays in the DOM: screen readers can reach it either way.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
